.Tech, or Bachelor of Technology, is a four-year undergraduate degree that focuses on engineering, technology, and practical problem-solving. It is one of the most popular courses for students who have completed their Class 12 with subjects such as Physics, Chemistry, and Mathematics. There are many branches of B.Tech, including Computer Science Engineering, Information Technology, Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning, Electronics and Communication Engineering, Electrical and Electronics Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Civil Engineering, and Chemical Engineering. Admission to B.Tech colleges is generally based on entrance examinations such as JEE Main, JEE Advanced, state-level entrance exams, or university-specific exams
